updated_at: "2026-08-08T11:45:02.529Z"
assignee: pi-agent
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "Every executable TypeScript file is instrumented at exact 100 percent for every supported coverage dimension with behavioral tests; ESLint enforces no explicit any, no inline or dynamic imports, erasable syntax, and package conventions; a strict duplicate-code gate runs; a raw physical commit and annotated-tag identity audit includes unreachable objects and permits only approved public identities; tracked files and full history pass secret and private-data scans; release:check and prepublishOnly fail closed on every gate"
definition_of_ready: "Inventory emitted sources, operational scripts, all physical Git identities, maintained TypeScript lint tooling, and duplicate-code tooling without printing private values"
value: Makes pm-rl's release-readiness claims literal and privacy-preserving
impact: "Prevents operational tooling, duplicated or forbidden code, and historical personal metadata from bypassing publication gates"
outcome: One fail-closed release command proves all-source quality and full-history privacy
why_now: "The 2026.8.7 compatibility audit proved the configured two-file gate but found three excluded scripts, two non-noreply history identities, and absent lint/duplication enforcement"
